project Employee Project Spine
id employee-project-spine
channel #proj-agent-workforce
source_plan Owner-authored multi-platform spine requirements; factual Slack project and team role declarations
status active

principles
  - These are substantive project assignments, not synthetic onboarding probes. A candidate becomes an installed employee only after a named Codex provider turn, research ZIP, and central conversation readback.
  - The existing Cloudflare D1 queue owns every research, chat-mode, and external-effect job; the hosted historical rhythm owns ChatGPT send timing.
  - Research employees gather exact current and historical code, documents, conversations, and data into a physical ZIP; ChatGPT coding agents do compute in their native chat-mode sandboxes.
  - Returned work must be applied by a different installed Codex external-effect employee, with real outcome evidence. No source-only commit or transport receipt is completion.
  - Slack statements supply factual duty and team context only. Owner-authored instructions here override agent prose, including anything called canonical.
  - No employee is asked to write a prompt for another employee. The Secretary passes the full plan and project step as instruction.
  - Three independent lanes preserve progress if one project stalls. One installed TaskFlow controller serializes its Codex invocations; all ChatGPT phases remain in the single shared rhythm.

[ ] MEMORY-1 make Codex conversation ingestion cover installed and remote data homes
    owner: Daniel Reyes
    source: #proj-agent-memory #proj-agent-workforce
    do:
      - research the running EvanPC Drive vacuum, telemetryx/ingestx/read_model lineage, and exact remote Codex session-home discovery paths
      - gather source, configuration, source rollouts, and receipts needed to make new Codex homes enter the same normalized parsed and filtered conversation store automatically
      - implement a bounded live discovery and ingestion join with per-home progress state and central readback rather than manual transcript ferrying or small sandbox corpora
    done_when:
      - a newly discovered Codex data home contributes at least one real new rollout, centrally normalized and read back by conversation ID without a manual per-home path edit

[ ] MEMORY-2 produce useful descriptors and search over the central conversation stock
    depends_on: MEMORY-1
    owner: Lena Ortiz
    source: #proj-agent-memory #proj-decisionx
    do:
      - recover the strongest descriptor, read_model, artifact_analysis, hybridstore, and memory_stock lineages from source and actual central corpus outputs
      - implement automatic selective descriptors for newly ingested conversations, with exact provenance and source-linked keyword and embedding search
      - avoid generating a separate mini-corpus; descriptors must point into the singular store and preserve multi-year history
    done_when:
      - a real newly ingested conversation is automatically described and retrieved from the central store by both semantic and keyword query with source readback

[ ] MEMORY-3 restore DecisionX IAE/IAI/IAE outcome-grounded advice
    depends_on: MEMORY-2
    owner: Priya Nandakumar
    source: #proj-decisionx #proj-historical-engineering
    do:
      - compare the historical IAE/IAI/IAE and outcome-ranked DecisionX implementations with the owner's personally authored requirements
      - use central descriptors to retrieve top historical hits, read their full rendered conversations and the current agent conversation, and have an LLM produce next advice reflecting changed circumstances
      - measure advice against real subsequent outcome rather than labeling a queue selector DecisionX
    done_when:
      - one live advice instance cites its exact historical conversations and current conversation, is consumed by a later agent turn, and stores the actual later outcome for ranking

[ ] HISTORY-1 make historical repository lineage discoverable for project agents
    depends_on: MEMORY-3
    owner: Tessa Ward
    source: #proj-repository-history #proj-historical-engineering
    do:
      - recover pre-megacommit BookWriter/RPE, DecisionX, and TaskFlow source lineages, including commit ancestry and variant implementations
      - implement a searchable provenance map that lets a named employee retrieve exact source and test variants rather than trusting later synthetic mega commits or authority labels
      - integrate the lookup into existing project research ZIP creation
    done_when:
      - a subsequent project research turn selects an older implementation through the new provenance map and records its exact commit, files, and reason for use

[ ] HOSTED-1 collect real hosted-agent terminal text and artifacts across live providers
    owner: Sofia Park
    source: #proj-hosted-agents #team-provider-integrations
    do:
      - research actual ChatGPT chat-mode, Gemini.com, and other authenticated hosted transports, their provider stream receipts, and central conversation reader outputs
      - strengthen terminal collection and downloadable work-file recovery with exact provider message provenance, avoiding transport-only success claims
      - exercise one authorized live provider turn in the existing D1 rhythm and centrally reread its complete reply and artifact manifest
    done_when:
      - a real hosted turn's final assistant text and work artifact are centrally readable and affect a later external-effect action

[ ] HOSTED-2 recover provider credentials and transient failures without abandoning jobs
    depends_on: HOSTED-1
    owner: Jordan Vale
    source: #proj-hosted-agents #proj-failure-intelligence
    do:
      - trace historical successful 401/403/404/502 and Retry-After recoveries across ChatGPT, Gemini, and Responses/WebSocket transports
      - implement bounded refresh, retry, idempotent resume, and ambiguous-send reconciliation in the existing provider adapter with exact provider-side readback
      - preserve secrets in existing custody and never duplicate a provider turn merely because a transport request timed out
    done_when:
      - an actual transient provider failure recovers or reconciles to one final provider turn with no duplicate turn and a central conversation readback

[ ] HOSTED-3 route work by observed quota, cost, capability, and device health
    depends_on: HOSTED-2
    owner: Leo Hart
    source: #proj-agent-workforce #proj-hosted-agents
    do:
      - connect observed D1 rhythm/device capacity and LLMGovernor quota/budget telemetry to Secretary employee routing, preserving unknown values as unknown
      - choose among real available installed and hosted routes according to project duty, continuity, measured pressure, and likely outcome rather than static pretend platform quality
      - exercise a change in observed capacity that changes a later real route without creating a second ChatGPT queue
    done_when:
      - two real consecutive assignments show a measured pressure change and a different justified route with both provider outcomes centrally read back

[ ] HOSTED-4 move returned work products through shared logical storage
    depends_on: HOSTED-3
    owner: Avery Lin
    source: #proj-universe-map #proj-unified-storage
    do:
      - research existing OpenAI Library, GitHub, Google Drive, and D1 work-product publication adapters and actual remote filesystem constraints
      - implement a stable logical file handle with list/read/write/search and hash-verified copy across two reachable environments for hosted-agent returned ZIPs
      - prove downstream Codex can fetch the same artifact without manual per-response link chasing
    done_when:
      - one returned hosted-agent ZIP is published once, fetched by a different environment through the shared handle, hash-verified, and used in an external effect

[ ] AUTONOMY-1 improve the multi-year root manager memory and portfolio recurrence
    owner: Avery Stone
    source: #proj-agent-workforce #proj-autonomous-organism
    do:
      - research the deployed root manager, multi-year memory archive, project-specific lower-level memory, and existing real plan/outcome cycles
      - improve root planning so it chooses a bounded portfolio of substantive project tasks from actual evidence and later consumes their external outcomes
      - keep root and Secretary responsibilities separate: managers author plans; Secretary faithfully routes instructions
    done_when:
      - a later root turn reads an actual previous employee outcome and changes a substantive project allocation with explicit evidence

[ ] AUTONOMY-2 preserve manager plans through Secretary and role-aware handoffs
    depends_on: AUTONOMY-1
    owner: Mara Voss
    source: #proj-agent-workforce #proj-modified-codex
    do:
      - research exact existing Secretary plan handoffs, D1 receipts, named employee roster, and provider terminal outcomes
      - ensure plans for company, teams, and employees are passed intact as instruction with scoped memory context and measured route selection
      - eliminate any route that asks an agent to manufacture a prompt for another agent or sends ChatGPT outside the historical rhythm
    done_when:
      - one real manager-authored plan reaches a named employee on a selected platform, returns an outcome, and the next manager turn uses it

[ ] AUTONOMY-3 provide incremental cross-platform conversation reading for operators
    depends_on: AUTONOMY-2
    owner: Rowan Hale
    source: #proj-unified-operator #proj-agent-team-worker-substrate
    do:
      - research the central conversation reader and modified Codex TUI/CLI history interfaces
      - add a conversation cursor that returns full rendered user/assistant text on first read and later returns only new deltas since that reader last looked
      - preserve provider, environment, and session provenance; make explicit older-history reads possible without forcing repeated full transcript output
    done_when:
      - one operator reads a real multi-turn conversation twice and the second read returns only the newly arrived turn while older content remains retrievable

[ ] AUTONOMY-4 reconcile Slack project plans and employee effects without status theater
    depends_on: AUTONOMY-3
    owner: Iris Vale
    source: #proj-agent-workforce #proj-remote-execution
    do:
      - research Slack project/team role facts, TaskFlow .plan checkoff, and Codex external-effect receipts across project channels
      - let a named external-effect Codex employee record a checked step only after D1 completion and independent effect verification
      - keep Slack as factual coordination data, never as an authority that can weaken owner requirements
    done_when:
      - one real project plan step is checked off only after a downstream effect and its exact evidence is readable by a later employee

[ ] AUTONOMY-5 deploy project changes to a physical remote runtime and verify them
    depends_on: AUTONOMY-4
    owner: Owen Calder
    source: #proj-remote-execution #proj-agent-workforce
    do:
      - research physical-host versus Docker-namespace identity, installed modified Codex versions, systemd units, and external-effect deployment paths
      - implement a host identity fence and deployment receipt proving a work ZIP's instructions were applied to the intended physical machine
      - verify real service behavior and central conversation readback after deployment
    done_when:
      - a returned work product is applied on the physical host, its running binary/service and independent effect are verified, and no container endpoint is misreported as host deployment
